W44-142: codec_wiki EPF seed suppression max_distance bisection
================================================================================

DATE: 2026-05-20
COMMIT: TBD (W44-142 ship commit on origin/main)
BASELINE: b8333091 (W44-140 SHIPPED, also same as `6a7d8835` main = W44-141 ledger)
HOST: lilith (water-cooled AMD Ryzen 9 7950X, 128 GB RAM)

PURPOSE
-------

Determine the W44-142 EPF seed suppression sub-gate's `max_distance`
threshold. The W44-141 cjxl-parity ledger refresh
(`benchmarks/cjxl_parity_ledger_2026-05-20_w44_141.{tsv,meta}`) surfaced
a NEW regression cluster on codec_wiki e8/e9 d=1.2/1.6/1.8 (SSIM2
deltas -0.60 to -0.72 vs W44-134 baseline). The W44-141 memo attributed
these to "W44-140 over-correction on mixed-content codec_wiki"; the
W44-142 investigation traced the actual mechanism per cell:

  - codec_wiki e9 d=1.2 -0.599 SSIM2: TRUE W44-140 fade-band collateral
    (fade weight=0.4 at d=1.2; current path is the 40% W44-117 / 60%
    uniform-4 blend; W44-141 memo attribution correct).
  - codec_wiki e8/e9 d=1.6/1.8 (-0.62 / -0.72): NOT W44-140 attributable.
    Bytes are byte-identical pre/post-W44-140 main at d>=1.5 (weight=1.0
    above fade_max). The bytes ARE different W134 vs W141 because of
    W44-135 (commit `2b9c98d0`, distance-gate W44-124 dct32_keep out of
    the d=1.0..1.8 band on codec_wiki). The W44-141 memo conflated
    W44-135's effect with W44-140's.

Goal: ship the narrowest possible W44-117/140 suppression gate that
closes the W44-140-attributable cell without touching cells outside the
fade band (so the residual W44-135 cluster stays as a follow-on chunk
without being made worse).

VARIANTS TESTED
---------------

Per-cell A/B/C/D mode interleaved, 24 cells × 4 modes:

  A_pre_w44_142 : JXL_W44_142_SUPPRESS_DISABLE=1 (current main W141)
  B_d15         : JXL_W44_142_SUPPRESS_MAX_DISTANCE=1.5 (= W44-140 fade upper edge)
  C_d17         : JXL_W44_142_SUPPRESS_MAX_DISTANCE=1.7 (covers e9 d=1.6 cell)
  D_d20         : JXL_W44_142_SUPPRESS_MAX_DISTANCE=2.0 (initial attempt; full coverage of W44-141 cluster)

All variants share the SAME content discriminator: m3>=60 AND ed<0.05
(identical to W44-124's dct32_keep auto-discriminator constants —
proven to cleanly admit codec_wiki and exclude every other gb82-sc
screen and every CID22 photo).

CELLS
-----

16 codec_wiki cells (e8/e9 × d ∈ {1.0, 1.2, 1.4, 1.5, 1.6, 1.8, 2.0, 3.0})
8 terminal cells (e8/e9 × d ∈ {1.0, 1.2, 1.4, 1.5, 1.6} + e9 × d ∈ {1.0, 1.2, 1.4})

Terminal protection set verifies that the m3 gate (terminal m3=13.85)
cleanly rejects terminal so the gate firing on codec_wiki never spills
to terminal byte-identical behaviour.

