ACCEPTANCE GATE (target cells: codec_wiki d=1.2/1.6/1.8 within ±0.10 of W134)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

| variant | cells within ±0.10 | new FIXED→OPEN-shape regressions |
|---------|--------------------|-----------------------------------|
| A       | 1 / 6 (only e8 d=1.2 close) | (baseline)            |
| **B**   | **2 / 6** (e9 d=1.2 closes; e8 d=1.2/1.8 ALREADY within at A) | **0** |
| C       | 3 / 6 (B's + e9 d=1.6 closes) | 1 (e8 d=1.6: -0.62 → -1.02) |
| D       | 3 / 6 (same as C) | 2 (e8 d=1.6 + e9 d=1.8 newly worse) |

B is pareto-optimal: closes the single W44-140-attributable cell (e9
d=1.2) without making anything worse. C closes one more cell but
introduces a -0.41 ssim2 regression on e8 d=1.6 (worse than W141 main
by -0.41, worse than W134 by -1.02). D regresses e8 d=1.8 by -0.76.

The e8/e9 split at d>=1.5 reflects the W44-117 / W44-140 mechanism
hitting a different equilibrium at e8 (2 buttloop iters) vs e9 (4
iters) on codec_wiki specifically. Pure threshold tightening cannot
resolve this — the same shape that drove the W44-140 fade design.

SHIPPING DECISION
-----------------

B (d<1.5) is the SHIP. Closes the only W44-140-attributable cluster
cell. Leaves codec_wiki d=1.6/1.8 byte-identical to current main —
those cells remain in the parity-ledger as residual inferiority, but
they are NOT W44-140-attributable (per the bisect data showing W44-117
firing OR not firing at d>=1.5 doesn't change the W141 baseline at
d=1.6/1.8). Future W44-143 chunk should investigate W44-135's
dct32_keep distance gate (`2b9c98d0`) as the actual source of those
regressions.

TERMINAL BYTE-IDENTICAL CHECK
-----------------------------

All 8 terminal cells (e8/e9 × d ∈ {1.0, 1.2, 1.4, 1.5, 1.6}):
A == B == C == D byte-identical.

The terminal m3=13.85 cleanly fails the m3>=60 gate, so the W44-142
suppression never fires on terminal regardless of the max_distance
cap. W44-140 wins fully preserved.

PHOTO PROTECTION (4 cells from earlier A/B harness, max_distance=2.0)
---------------------------------------------------------------------

From `benchmarks/w44_142_codec_wiki_suppress_ab_2026-05-20.tsv`
(initial A/B at d=2.0): all 4 photo cells (1418519 e8 d=2/5, 1025469
e8 d=2/5) are byte-identical between A and B. ed >= 0.16 on all CID22
photos rejects them via the ed gate. The shipped d<1.5 cap further
narrows the band so even if ed were lower, the gate's distance window
[1.0, 1.5) does not overlap typical photo bench distances >= 2.0.

DO NOT
------

- DO NOT raise W44_142_EPF_SEED_SUPPRESS_MAX_DISTANCE above 1.5. The
  bisect is conclusive: max_distance ∈ {1.7, 2.0} introduce -0.4 to
  -0.8 SSIM2 regressions on codec_wiki e8 d=1.6/1.8 cells that current
  main does NOT have. The W44-141 memo's "fix the cluster" framing
  conflates W44-140's effect at d=1.2 with W44-135's effect at
  d=1.6/1.8 — only the d=1.2 cell is actually inside the W44-140 fade
  band and addressable by an EPF-seed-tier change.

- DO NOT lower W44_142_EPF_SEED_SUPPRESS_M3_MIN below 60. The W44-124
  probe established that imessage (m3=67.65, ed=0.0533) would slip
  through if m3<60 OR ed>=0.05; the W44-123 measurement showed
  imessage regresses under high_d_photo_lift firing on it.

- DO NOT raise W44_142_EPF_SEED_SUPPRESS_EDGE_DENSITY_MAX above 0.05.
  Same rationale — imessage at 0.0533 must stay out.

- DO NOT respawn FMA precision claims (binding directive per
  cardinal_rule + fd_residual_not_fma_precision memos).

REPRODUCER
----------

CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$HOME/work/zen/jxl-encoder-shared-target \
  cargo run --release \
  --features 'parallel butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop' \
  --example w44_142_max_distance_bisect \
  --manifest-path jxl-encoder/Cargo.toml \
  > benchmarks/w44_142_max_distance_bisect_2026-05-20.tsv

Wall time: 1011.4 s (24 cells × 4 modes × encode + decode + butteraugli + ssim2).

